INT. VERTICAL FARM BREAK ROOM - FLUORESCENT PINK LIGHT - DAY

Under the grow-lamp glow, everyone looks sunburned and sick. Racks of lettuce climb the walls behind the vending machine. A sign on the fridge reads: THIS IS NOT A COMMUNAL FRIDGE. IT IS A FRIDGE OF COMMUNITY.

PRIYANKA DESAI, thirties, Head of Culture, slides a cake onto the table with candles shaped like leaves. NATHANIEL "NAT" OYELOWO, forties, a quiet agronomist, stands near the sink in a fleece vest. WILHELMINA "BILLIE" STOCKTON, twenties, new hire, hovers by the door holding a tote bag.

PRIYANKA
Surprise! Welcome, Billie!

BILLIE
Oh my gosh. You didn't have to.

PRIYANKA
We always do. Right, Nat?

NAT
(flatly)
We did for the last four.

Priyanka laughs a half-second too long. Billie smiles and sets her bag on the counter.

BILLIE
Where do I... put my lunch?

She opens the fridge. Inside, every shelf is labeled with a name. One shelf has a pink sticky note: BILLIE'S, in Priyanka's handwriting. Another, in Nat's: FORMER BILLIE'S.

Billie looks at the note. She looks at Nat. Nat looks at the lettuce.

BILLIE (CONT'D)
Who was the former Billie?

PRIYANKA
Nobody. A joke. Cake?

She hands Billie a plate. She takes it with both hands, politely, and turns to Nat.

BILLIE
Did she quit, or...

NAT
(softly)
She harvested.
